                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>DCMONITORIQSEL</name>
                <description>Selects which part of the 32 bit register hoding the dcmonitori/q value is read out from the DCMONITORI/Q field of the register SCPDCMONITORI/Q.
          Only valid for 16-bit SCP, unused by 12-bit SCP.</description>
                <lsb>1</lsb>
                <msb>1</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Lower16BitsAreReadOu</name>
                    <description>Lower 16 bits are read out from the DCMONITORI/Q[15:0] field.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Upper16BitsAreReadOu</name>
                    <description>Upper 16 bits are read out from the DCMONITORI/Q[15:0] field.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>LOBASE</name>
            <description>SCP LO BASE</description>
            <addressOffset>0x100</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>LOBASE</name>
                <description>Local Oscillator base. This is an unsigned value which is combined with LOCONTROL to generate the 26-bit control Fc:
          Fc = (LOBASE &amp;lt;&amp;lt; 23) + LOCONTROL
          Fc is in 2's complement signed format where its value represents numbers within the range -1 to 0.9999999. To convert a ratio into the 26-bit Fc, multiply by 2^25.
          The digitally generated Local Oscillator (LO) frequency used in the mixer section is equal to Fc * (IF Clock Frequency/2). Hence the full-scale negative value represents a frequency of -(IF Clock Frequency/2).
          The input signal is frequency translated such that input frequency F moves to a frequency of F + Local Oscillator (LO) Frequency.
          NOTE : a real IF input implicitly carries the inverse of its positive spectrum at negative frequencies. This means that a positive Fc applied to a real IF gives an inverted spectrum, and a negative Fc gives a non-inverted one. An SCP input contains independent positive and negative frequency components, so Fc cannot invert the spectrum.</description>
                <lsb>21</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>LOCONTROL</name>
            <description>SCP LO CONTROL</description>
            <addressOffset>0x104</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>LOCONTROL</name>
                <description>Local Oscillator control. This is a 2's complement value which is combined with LOBASE to generate the 26-bit control Fc:
          Fc = (LOBASE &amp;lt;&amp;lt; 23) + LOCONTROL</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>MIXERBYPASS</name>
            <description>SCP MIXER BYPASS</description>
            <addressOffset>0x10C</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
