            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>APPLYPARAMETERSB</name>
                <description>If the SYNCHRONISEUPDATES bit is set in the Control register, a number of parameters are updated synchronously when the sample number is equal to (APPLYPARAMETERSB - 1). Thus, with the control bit set, writes to the parameter fields are held off until SAMPLENUMBERB = (APPLYPARAMETERSB - 1). If SYNCHRONISEUPDATES is not set, updates to the parameters occur immediately that they are written to the appropriate registers.The following parameter updates are synchronized:
          The following parameter updates are synchronized:
          - GAINCONTROL1
          - GAINCONTROL2
          - OFFSETCONTROL1
          - OFFSETCONTROL2
          - DCOFFSETI
          - DCOFFSETQ
          - COARSEGAIN
          - IGAIN
          - QGAIN
          - ITOQGAIN
          - FS
          - FC</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
