          <cluster>
            <dim>2</dim>
            <dimIncrement>0x008</dimIncrement>
            <name>LATEGAINLUT[%s]</name>
            <description>Unspecified</description>
            <headerStructName>WIFIPHY_SCP_LATEGAINLUT</headerStructName>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <addressOffset>0x3B0</addressOffset>
            <register>
              <name>LATEFINEGAINI</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP LATE FINE GAIN I</description>
              <addressOffset>0x000</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00200000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>LATEIGAIN</name>
                  <description>2's complement value that multiplies I value from SCP. This is a linear gain where 0x100 represents the 0dB point, thus the fine gain is LATEIGAIN/0x100.</description>
                  <lsb>13</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
              <name>LATEFINEGAINQ</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP LATE FINE GAIN Q</description>
              <addressOffset>0x004</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00200000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>LATEQGAIN</name>
                  <description>2's complement value that multiplies Q value from SCP. This is a linear gain where 0x100 represents the 0dB point, thus the fine gain is LATEQGAIN/0x100.</description>
                  <lsb>13</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
          </cluster>
          <cluster>
            <dim>4</dim>
            <dimIncrement>0x008</dimIncrement>
            <name>MIXERLUT[%s]</name>
            <description>Unspecified</description>
            <headerStructName>WIFIPHY_SCP_MIXERLUT</headerStructName>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <addressOffset>0x3C0</addressOffset>
            <register>
              <name>LOBASE</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP LO BASE</description>
              <addressOffset>0x000</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>LOBASE</name>
                  <description>Local Oscillator base. This is an unsigned value which is combined with LOCONTROL to generate the 26-bit control Fc:
          Fc = (LOBASE &amp;lt;&amp;lt; 23) + LOCONTROL
          Fc is in 2's complement signed format where its value represents numbers within the range -1 to 0.9999999. To convert a ratio into the 26-bit Fc, multiply by 2^25.
          The digitally generated Local Oscillator (LO) frequency used in the mixer section is equal to Fc * (IF Clock Frequency/2). Hence the full-scale negative value represents a frequency of -(IF Clock Frequency/2).
          The input signal is frequency translated such that input frequency F moves to a frequency of F + Local Oscillator (LO) Frequency.
          NOTE : a real IF input implicitly carries the inverse of its positive spectrum at negative frequencies. This means that a positive Fc applied to a real IF gives an inverted spectrum, and a negative Fc gives a non-inverted one. An SCP input contains independent positive and negative frequency components, so Fc cannot invert the spectrum.</description>
                  <lsb>21</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
              <name>LOCONTROL</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP LO CONTROL</description>
              <addressOffset>0x004</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>LOCONTROL</name>
                  <description>Local Oscillator control. This is a 2's complement value which is combined with LOBASE to generate the 26-bit control Fc:
          Fc = (LOBASE &amp;lt;&amp;lt; 23) + LOCONTROL</description>
                  <lsb>0</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
          </cluster>
          <cluster>
            <dim>4</dim>
            <dimIncrement>0x008</dimIncrement>
            <name>RESAMPLERLUT[%s]</name>
            <description>Unspecified</description>
            <headerStructName>WIFIPHY_SCP_RESAMPLERLUT</headerStructName>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <addressOffset>0x3E0</addressOffset>
            <register>
              <name>RESAMPLINGFACTORBASE</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP RESAMPLING FACTOR BASE</description>
              <addressOffset>0x000</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00800000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>RESAMPBASE</name>
                  <description>Resampling factor base. This is an unsigned value which is combined with the 2's complement RESAMPCONTROL to generate the 26-bit control Fs:
          Fs = (RESAMPBASE &amp;lt;&amp;lt; 23) + RESAMPCONTROL
          Fs is the sample conversion ratio (I / O) used in the sample rate conversion section of the SCP.
          Fs is an unsigned number, where the full-scale range of values is 1 / (2^25) to ((2^26) - 1) / (2^25) = 2.98023224E-08 to 1.99999997
          NOTE: To convert a ratio into the 26-bit Fs, multiply by 2^25</description>
                  <lsb>21</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
            <register>
              <name>RESAMPLINGFACTORCONTROL</name>
              <description>Description cluster: SCP RESAMPLING FACTOR CONTROL</description>
              <addressOffset>0x004</addressOffset>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
              <size>0x20</size>
              <fields>
                <field>
                  <name>RESAMPCONTROL</name>
                  <description>Resampling factor control. This is a 2's complement value which is combined with RESAMPBASE to generate the 26-bit control Fs:
          Fs = (RESAMPBASE &amp;lt;&amp;lt; 23) + RESAMPCONTROL</description>
                  <lsb>0</lsb>
                  <msb>23</msb>
                </field>
              </fields>
            </register>
          </cluster>
        </cluster>
        <cluster>
          <name>WLANCTRL</name>
