          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANAGCLGCCONFIG10</name>
            <description>WLAN AGC LGC CONFIG 10</description>
            <addressOffset>0x6C</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00152F58</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>LGLNASWITCHPOINTTABLE0</name>
                <description>lnaSwitchPointDbm for LNA stage 0, where lnaSwitchPointDbm is defined as:
          The value of RF input power in dBm which meets the following equation:
          rfRssiVal3Bit = lnaSwitchPointDbm + LGRSSIINCRPOWERFACTOR * (rfInPowerDbm - lnaSwitchPointDbm).
          This value is 7-bit signed. Default value is -40.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>6</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LGLNASWITCHPOINTTABLE1</name>
                <description>lnaSwitchPointDbm for LNA stage 1, where lnaSwitchPointDbm is defined as:
          The value of RF input power in dBm which meets the following equation:
          rfRssiVal3Bit = lnaSwitchPointDbm + LGRSSIINCRPOWERFACTOR * (rfInPowerDbm - lnaSwitchPointDbm).
          This value is 7-bit signed. Default value is -34.</description>
                <lsb>7</lsb>
                <msb>13</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LGLNASWITCHPOINTTABLE2</name>
                <description>lnaSwitchPointDbm for LNA stage 2, where lnaSwitchPointDbm is defined as:
          The value of RF input power in dBm which meets the following equation:
          rfRssiVal3Bit = lnaSwitchPointDbm + LGRSSIINCRPOWERFACTOR * (rfInPowerDbm - lnaSwitchPointDbm).
          This value is 7-bit signed. Default value is -28.</description>
                <lsb>14</lsb>
                <msb>20</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANAGCLGCCONFIG11</name>
            <description>WLAN AGC LGC CONFIG 11</description>
            <addressOffset>0x70</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00003E70</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>LGLNASWITCHPOINTTABLE3</name>
                <description>lnaSwitchPointDbm for LNA stage 3, where lnaSwitchPointDbm is defined as:
          The value of RF input power in dBm which meets the following equation:
          rfRssiVal3Bit = lnaSwitchPointDbm + LGRSSIINCRPOWERFACTOR * (rfInPowerDbm - lnaSwitchPointDbm).
          This value is 7-bit signed. Default value is -16.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>6</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LGLNASWITCHPOINTTABLE4</name>
                <description>lnaSwitchPointDbm for LNA stage 4, where lnaSwitchPointDbm is defined as:
          The value of RF input power in dBm which meets the following equation:
          rfRssiVal3Bit = lnaSwitchPointDbm + LGRSSIINCRPOWERFACTOR * (rfInPowerDbm - lnaSwitchPointDbm).
          This value is 7-bit signed. Default value is -4.</description>
                <lsb>7</lsb>
                <msb>13</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>LGRSSIDONETIMEOUT</name>
                <description>The count in number of ADC input samples before the the wait for the RF RSSI done is aborted along with LNA search operation.
          It has a range of 0 .. 127. Default value is 0.
          Timeout check is disabled when LGRSSIDONETIMEOUT = 0.</description>
                <lsb>14</lsb>
                <msb>20</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANAGCMONITOR</name>
            <description>WLAN AGC MONITOR</description>
            <addressOffset>0x74</addressOffset>
            <access>read-only</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>BTFREEZE</name>
                <description>Input signal from BT module where '1' indicates the BT wants the LNA gain not to be changed.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>0</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Disable</name>
                    <description>Disable</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Enable</name>
                    <description>Enable</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>EDPACKETDETECTED</name>
                <description>'1' indicates either OFDM/DSSS packet has been detected and TD processing is in progress.</description>
                <lsb>1</lsb>
                <msb>1</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>EDACIDETECTED</name>
                <description>ACI detected signal from ED module. This can be used for freezing the AGC gain. So that AGC doesn't enter trigger-&amp;gt;search-&amp;gt;settle cycle multiple times, thereby reducing the blind period.</description>
                <lsb>2</lsb>
                <msb>2</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>RFRSSIDONE</name>
                <description>From RF module, indicates the completion of RSSI value computation.</description>
                <lsb>3</lsb>
                <msb>3</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>RFRSSIVALUE</name>
                <description>From RF module, the 3-bit RF RSSI value where a higher value like 7 indicates severe saturation at LNA output. This is an 3-bit signed.</description>
                <lsb>4</lsb>
                <msb>6</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>AGCSAMPLEID</name>
                <description>AGC sample index.</description>
                <lsb>7</lsb>
                <msb>22</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
