          It is defined as WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2NROWS multiplied by WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2NCOLS - the value in this register is ONLY valid when it is derived from valid values in those two registers.</description>
                <lsb>11</lsb>
                <msb>19</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2CONSTMAPMODE</name>
                <description>Specifies the constellation mapping mode.  Valid values are below.  Other values are reserved and should not be used.
          Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0. Note mapping mode of 256-QAM is only valid if WLANTXPWIFIACSUPPORT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>20</lsb>
