              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPLDPCCONTROL</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP LDPC CONTROL</description>
            <addressOffset>0x20</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCZBLOCKSIZE</name>
                <description>Selects the Z-block size of the LDPC encoder. Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1.
          Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>1</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>ZBlockSize27Bits</name>
                    <description>Z-Block Size 27 bits.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>ZBlockSize54Bits</name>
                    <description>Z-Block Size 54 bits.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>ZBlockSize81Bits</name>
                    <description>Z-Block Size 81 bits.</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>InvalidValue</name>
                    <description>Invalid value.</description>
                    <value>0x3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCNUMPARITYREPETITIONBLOCKS</name>
                <description>Defines the number of LDPC blocks equal to or below which:
          1) The number of parity bits is 1 less than the value configured in WLANTXPLDPCPARITYBITS if WLANTXPLDPCREPETITIONACTIVE is 0.
          2) The number of repetition bits is 1 more than the value configured in WLANTXPLDPCREPETITIONBITS if WLANTXPLDPCREPETITIONACTIVE is 1.
          Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1. Note :
          1) This field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.
          2) Represents values in the range 0 to 65535 if WLANTXPWIFIACSUPPORT = 1 or 0 to 1023 otherwise.</description>
                <lsb>4</lsb>
                <msb>19</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPLDPCNUMMESSAGEBLOCKS</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP LDPC NUM MESSAGE BLOCKS</description>
            <addressOffset>0x24</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCNUMMESSAGEBLOCKS</name>
                <description>Defines the number of LDPC blocks equal to or below which the number of message bits is 1 less than the value configured in WLANTXPLDPCMESSAGEBITS. Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1.
          Note:
          1) This field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.
          2) Represents values in the range 0 to 65535 if WLANTXPWIFIACSUPPORT = 1 or 0 to 1023 otherwise.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>15</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPLDPCMESSAGEPARITYBITS</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP LDPC MESSAGE PARITY BITS</description>
            <addressOffset>0x28</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCMESSAGEBITS</name>
                <description>Defines the number of valid message bits in k information bits of a LDPC code word, the remaining bits are zero padded in order to perform block encoding (shortening).
          Value written to this field and WLANTXPLDPCNUMMESSAGEBLOCKS should be chosen such that the number of valid message bits lie in the range 1 to k-bits. Where the maximum value of k-bits supported by the code word can be obtained from WLANTXPLDPCZBLOCKSIZE and WLANTXPLDPCCODERATE.
          Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1. Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>10</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCPARITYBITS</name>
                <description>Defines the number of valid parity bits in (n-k) parity bits of a LDPC code word, the remaining bits are discarded. Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1.
          Note :
          1) Value written to this field and WLANTXPLDPCNUMPARITYREPETITIONBLOCKS should be chosen such that the number of valid parity bits lie in the range 1 to (n-k)-bits. Where the maximum value of (n-k)-bits supported by the code word can be obtained from WLANTXPLDPCZBLOCKSIZE and WLANTXPLDPCCODERATE.
          2) In case WLANTXPLDPCREPETITIONACTIVE is 1 the number of valid parity bits has to be equal to the maximum value of (n-k) bits.
          3) This field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>12</lsb>
                <msb>22</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPLDPCREPETITION</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP LDPC REPETITION</description>
            <addressOffset>0x2C</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCREPETITIONBITS</name>
                <description>Defines the number of repetition bits to be given out by the LDPC encoder after the message and parity bits. Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0, WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1 and WLANTXPLDPCREPETITIONACTIVE is set to 1.
          Repetition starts with the first valid message bits and continues with the valid parity bits. The valid message and parity bits are resent in this order until the required number of repetition bits have been sent out of the LDPC encoder.
          Note:
          1) This field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.
          2) Note the value written to this field and WLANTXPLDPCNUMPARITYREPETITIONBLOCKS should be chosen such that the number of repetition bits lie in the range 1 to 65535 if WLANTXPWIFIACSUPPORT = 1 or 1 to 8191 otherwise.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>15</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCREPETITIONACTIVE</name>
                <description>Selects if the message and parity bits need to be repeated. Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1.
          Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>23</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>RepetitionInActive</name>
                    <description>Repetition In-active.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>RepetitionActive</name>
                    <description>Repetition Active.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <dim>0x30</dim>
            <dimIncrement>0x4</dimIncrement>
            <name>WLANTXPLDPCHSUBROTATION[%s]</name>
            <description>Description collection: WLAN TXP LDPC H SUB ROTATION</description>
            <addressOffset>0x30</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x007F7F7F</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCHSUBROTATION0</name>
                <description>Defines the amount of right cyclic shift that needs to be performed on the 3n identity sub-matrix to form the H (parity check) matrix. Valid range is 0 to the Z-block size defined by WLANTXPLDPCZBLOCKSIZE. Value of 127 defines a null matrix.
          Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1. Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>6</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCHSUBROTATION1</name>
                <description>Defines the amount of right cyclic shift that needs to be performed on the 3n + 1 identity sub-matrix to form the H (parity check) matrix. Valid range is 0 to the Z-block size defined by WLANTXPLDPCZBLOCKSIZE. Value of 127 defines a null matrix.
          Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1. Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>14</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPLDPCHSUBROTATION2</name>
                <description>Defines the amount of right cyclic shift that needs to be performed on the 3n + 2 identity sub-matrix to form the H (parity check) matrix. Valid range is 0 to the Z-block size defined by WLANTXPLDPCZBLOCKSIZE. Value of 127 defines a null matrix.
          Relevant when WLANTXPTXMODE is 0 and WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 1. Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPLDPCENCODERPRESENT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>16</lsb>
                <msb>22</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPAGGRMPDUDELIMITER</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP AGGR MPDU DELIMITER</description>
            <addressOffset>0xF4</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRMPDUDELIMITER</name>
                <description>Defines the first 16 bits of MPDU delimiter</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>15</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPAGGRNUMFLUSHBYTES</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP AGGR NUM FLUSH BYTES</description>
            <addressOffset>0xF8</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRNUMFLUSHBYTES</name>
                <description>Defines the number of zero flush bytes that need to be added by the TXP Aggregation module at the end of a field. Represents values in the range 0 - 1023.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>9</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPAGGRNUMPAYLOADBYTES</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP AGGR NUM PAYLOAD BYTES</description>
            <addressOffset>0xFC</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRNUMPAYLOADBYTES</name>
                <description>Defines the number of payload bytes (including 4 byte of CRC-32 if WLANTXPAGGRADDCRC32 is 1) that need to be sent as part of MPDU data by the TXP Aggregation.
          Represents values in the range 0 - 1048575.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>19</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPAGGRSERVICEBYTES</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP AGGR SERVICE BYTES</description>
            <addressOffset>0x100</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRSERVICEBYTES</name>
                <description>Defines the first service byte that needs to be added to the output of the TXP Aggregation module, where:
          1) Bits [7-0] represent the first byte which is needed to compute the descrambler initial state.
          2) Bits [15-8] represent the second byte which is the CRC-8 computed over VHT Sig-B field or zero for formats other than VHT.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>15</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPCHBWINNONHTENABLE</name>
                <description>Defines the service byte output from the scrambler, where:
          Note this is only relevant for VHT packets.</description>
                <lsb>16</lsb>
                <msb>16</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>First7ServiceBitsAft</name>
                    <description>First 7 service bits after scrambling will be the state of the LFSR (scrambler seed) after 7 cycles.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>First7ServiceBitsWil</name>
                    <description>First 7 service bits will be the scrambler seed.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPAGGRNUMNULLMPDU</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP AGGR NUM NULL MPDU</description>
            <addressOffset>0x104</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRNUMNULLMPDU</name>
                <description>Defines the number of zero length MPDUs with:
          1) EOF set to 0 that need to be added between two consecutive MPDUs in an A-MPDU to provide the minimum MPDU Start Spacing field.
          2) EOF set to 1 that need to be added after the last non-zero length MPDU to provide EOF padding.
          Sent by the TXP Aggregation.
          Represents values in the range 0 - 262143.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>17</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPAGGRCONTROL</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP AGGR CONTROL</description>
            <addressOffset>0x108</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRADDDELIMITER</name>
                <description>Defines whether MPDU Delimiter needs to be transferred before MPDU data to form an A-MPDU subframe by the TXP Aggregation.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>0</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>MpduDelimiterNotTran</name>
                    <description>MPDU Delimiter not transferred.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>MpduDelimiterTransfe</name>
                    <description>MPDU Delimiter transferred.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRADDCRC32</name>
                <description>Enable or Disable CRC-32 computation on the MPDU data in the TXP Aggregation.</description>
                <lsb>1</lsb>
                <msb>1</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Crc32NotComputed</name>
                    <description>CRC-32 not computed.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Crc32ComputedAndApp</name>
                    <description>CRC-32 computed and appended after payload.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRNUMPADBYTES</name>
                <description>Defines the number of zero pad bytes that need to be appended after the MPDU data for all A-MPDU sub-frames by the TXP Aggregation, except the last one, so that the (WLANTXPAGGRNUMPAYLOADBYTES + WLANTXPAGGRNUMPADBYTES) is a multiple of 4.
          Represents values in the range 0 - 3.</description>
                <lsb>2</lsb>
                <msb>3</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRNUMEOFPADBYTES</name>
                <description>Defines the number of zero pad bytes that need to be appended after the last A-MPDU sub-frame by the TXP Aggregation to make A-MPDU length equal to PSDU length or a multiple of 4, whichever occurs first.
          Represents values in the range 0 - 3.</description>
                <lsb>4</lsb>
                <msb>5</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRTXFIELD</name>
                <description>Selects the field for which TXP Aggregation is being configured.
          Note if VHT Sig-B field is being processed the input data is sent to the TXP Aggregation circular buffer. TXP Aggregation should only receive 4 input bytes in this case.
          Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPWIFIACSUPPORT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>10</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>LegacyOrHt</name>
                    <description>Legacy or HT (High Throughput) fields.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Vht</name>
                    <description>VHT (Very High Throughput) all other fields.</description>
                    <value>0x3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Vht4</name>
                    <description>VHT (Very High Throughput) Sig-B field  20 MHz,  4 bytes taken out of the TXP Aggregation.</description>
                    <value>0x4</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Vht5</name>
                    <description>VHT (Very High Throughput) Sig-B field  40 MHz,  7 bytes taken out of the TXP Aggregation.</description>
                    <value>0x5</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Vht6</name>
                    <description>VHT (Very High Throughput) Sig-B field  80 MHz, 15 bytes taken out of the TXP Aggregation.</description>
                    <value>0x6</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Vht7</name>
                    <description>VHT (Very High Throughput) Sig-B field 160 MHz, 30 bytes taken out of the TXP Aggregation.</description>
                    <value>0x7</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRVHTBITINDEX</name>
                <description>Selects the bit index from which tail bit zero forcing of the output of the OFDM scrambler is enabled for the first flush bytes sent out of the TXP Aggregation at the end of a field.
          Relevant when WLANTXPAGGRTXFIELD is 011 - 111; WLANTXPENCODERSELECT is 0; and WLANTXPAGGRNUMFLUSHBYTES is not 0.
          Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPWIFIACSUPPORT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>11</lsb>
                <msb>13</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPAGGRBYPASS</name>
                <description>Causes the TXP Aggregation to be bypassed.</description>
                <lsb>23</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>AggregationNormalOpe</name>
                    <description>Aggregation normal operation.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>AggregationBypassed</name>
                    <description>Aggregation bypassed.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXP11BMODECONTROL</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP 11B MODE CONTROL</description>
            <addressOffset>0x10C</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXP11BPACKETFORMAT</name>
                <description>Selects the 802.11b data packet format.
          Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPWIFI11BSUPPORT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>0</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>LongDataPacketFormat</name>
                    <description>Long data packet format.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>ShortDataPacketForma</name>
                    <description>Short data packet format.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXP11BDATARATE</name>
                <description>Selects the transmission data rate.
          Note this field is only valid if WLANTXPWIFI11BSUPPORT = 1.</description>
                <lsb>1</lsb>
                <msb>2</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>1Mbps</name>
                    <description>1 Mbps.</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>2Mbps</name>
                    <description>2 Mbps.</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>55Mbps</name>
                    <description>5.5 Mbps.</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>11Mbps</name>
                    <description>11 Mbps.</description>
                    <value>0x3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXP11BLOCKEDCLOCKS</name>
                <description>Indicates that the transmit frequency and symbol clocks are derived from the same oscillator. This bit shall be set by the PHY layer based on its implementation configuration.</description>
                <lsb>3</lsb>
                <msb>3</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1CONTROL2</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP INTERLEAVER 1 CONTROL 2</description>
            <addressOffset>0x110</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIREADPOINTER</name>
                <description>Registers WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINIROWSWAPTYPE/INICOLOFFSET/INIROWOFFSET/INIREADPOINTER control Stage 3 interleaving.  To turn off Hardware Stage 3 interleaving set all four registers to 0.  To turn on Hardware Stage 3 interleaving configure all four registers correctly with non-zero values.
          This register specifies the initial value of the read pointer for reading the first element of bits from the read buffer.
          The value in this register is calculated as follows:
          ((WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINIROWOFFSET * WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnNCOLS) + WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET)</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>7</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIROWOFFSET</name>
                <description>Registers WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINIROWSWAPTYPE/INICOLOFFSET/INIROWOFFSET/INIREADPOINTER control Stage 3 interleaving.  To turn off Hardware Stage 3 interleaving set all four registers to 0.  To turn on Hardware Stage 3 interleaving configure all four registers correctly with non-zero values.
          Stage 3 Interleaver, Initial Row Offset. This is the row which holds the first Nbpsc read bits after rotation has been applied.  Note that a Row is made up of elements, each element holds Nbpsc bits.
          Row Offset is computed from the equation in section 2.2.3 (Third interleaver stage), is given in Table 3.
          Note 1. WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINIROWOFFSET has the range 0 to WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnNROWS-1
          Note 2. The valid values for this register can be found in the HW TRM, see section 7.4.9 (TXP Interleaver).  These are derived from the Row Offset equation in the same location.</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>11</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INICOLOFFSET</name>
                <description>Registers WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINIROWSWAPTYPE/INICOLOFFSET/INIROWOFFSET/INIREADPOINTER control Stage 3 interleaving.  To turn off Hardware Stage 3 interleaving set all four registers to 0.  To turn on Hardware Stage 3 interleaving configure all four registers correctly with non-zero values.
          Stage 3 Interleaver, Initial Column offset.  This is the column which holds the first Nbpsc read bits after rotation has been applied.  Note that a Column is made up of elements, each element holds Nbpsc bits.
          Note 1. WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET has the range 0 to WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnNCOLS-1.
          Note 2. The valid values for this register can be found in the HW TRM, see section 7.4.9 (TXP Interleaver).  These are derived from the Row Offset equation in the same location.</description>
                <lsb>12</lsb>
                <msb>16</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIROWSWAPTYPE</name>
                <description>Registers WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINIROWSWAPTYPE/INICOLOFFSET/INIROWOFFSET/INIREADPOINTER control Stage 3 interleaving.  To turn off Hardware Stage 3 interleaving set all four registers to 0.  To turn on Hardware Stage 3 interleaving configure all four registers correctly with non-zero values.
          This register is used to specify the row swapping type in use in the column WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET.  It is only used when the modulation, set in register WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnCONSTMAPMODE, is set to a modulation scheme that requires row swapping - i.e. not BPSK (Nbpsc = 1) or QPSK (Nbpsc = 2).
          The value in this register is calculated as follows:
          
          For  16-QAM (Nbpsc = 4): WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET percent2
          i.e. 0x0 when WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET is an even number
          
          For  64-QAM (Nbpsc = 6): WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET percent3
          i.e. 0x0 when WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET is 0,3,6, 9,12,etc
          
          For 256-QAM (Nbpsc = 8): WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET percent4
          i.e. 0x0 when WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET is 0,4, 8,12,etc</description>
                <lsb>20</lsb>
                <msb>21</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>WhenWlanTxpInterle</name>
                    <description>when WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET is 1,4,7,10,13,etc</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>WhenWlanTxpInterle2</name>
                    <description>when WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET is 2,5,8,11,14,etc</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>WhenWlanTxpInterle3</name>
                    <description>when WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnINICOLOFFSET is 3,7,11,15,etc</description>
                    <value>0x3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1LDPCMODE</name>
                <description>Defines the data processing mode when WLANTXPENCODERSELECT=1 (i.e. LDPC Encoder is selected).
          When WLANTXPENCODERSELECT=0 this register setting is not relevant.</description>
                <lsb>23</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>LdpcToneMappingNotEn</name>
                    <description>LDPC Tone Mapping not enabled.  Bypass the Interleaver logic such that received data is output unmodified (i.e. non-VHT frames)</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>LdpcToneMappingEnabl</name>
                    <description>LDPC Tone Mapping enabled.  Apply LDPC Tone Mapping to data received in the Interleaver as configured in register WLANTXPINTERLEAVERnCONTROL (i.e. VHT frames).</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2CONTROL2</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP INTERLEAVER 2 CONTROL 2</description>
            <addressOffset>0x114</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2INIREADPOINTER</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIREADPOINTER</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>7</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2INIROWOFFSET</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIROWOFFSET</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>11</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2INICOLOFFSET</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INICOLOFFSET</description>
                <lsb>12</lsb>
                <msb>16</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2INIROWSWAPTYPE</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIROWSWAPTYPE</description>
                <lsb>20</lsb>
                <msb>21</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER2LDPCMODE</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1LDPCMODE</description>
                <lsb>23</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER3CONTROL2</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP INTERLEAVER 3 CONTROL 2</description>
            <addressOffset>0x118</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER3INIREADPOINTER</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIREADPOINTER</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>7</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER3INIROWOFFSET</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIROWOFFSET</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>11</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER3INICOLOFFSET</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INICOLOFFSET</description>
                <lsb>12</lsb>
                <msb>16</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER3INIROWSWAPTYPE</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIROWSWAPTYPE</description>
                <lsb>20</lsb>
                <msb>21</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER3LDPCMODE</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1LDPCMODE</description>
                <lsb>23</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER4CONTROL2</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP INTERLEAVER 4 CONTROL 2</description>
            <addressOffset>0x11C</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER4INIREADPOINTER</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIREADPOINTER</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>7</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER4INIROWOFFSET</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIROWOFFSET</description>
                <lsb>8</lsb>
                <msb>11</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER4INICOLOFFSET</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INICOLOFFSET</description>
                <lsb>12</lsb>
                <msb>16</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER4INIROWSWAPTYPE</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1INIROWSWAPTYPE</description>
                <lsb>20</lsb>
                <msb>21</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPINTERLEAVER4LDPCMODE</name>
                <description>For description see WLANTXPINTERLEAVER1LDPCMODE</description>
                <lsb>23</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
          <register>
            <name>WLANTXPMAPPERANDPILOTCONTROL</name>
            <description>WLAN TXP MAPPER AND PILOT CONTROL</description>
            <addressOffset>0x120</addressOffset>
            <access>read-write</access>
            <resetValue>0x00040000</resetValue>
            <size>0x20</size>
            <fields>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPRESOURCEUNITALLOCATION</name>
                <description>Used to determine the number of non null sub-carriers.
          Valid ranges of values are [0-8, 9-17, 37-40, 41-44, 53-56, 61-62, 65].
          Only applicable for HE packets.</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>6</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPPACKETTYPE</name>
                <description>Selects packet type:
          Packets 0-3 (Legacy, HTMF, HTGF, VHT) are in Pre-HE group with OFDM symbol
          length of 3.2us. HE packets have 12.8us OFDM symbol length.</description>
                <lsb>7</lsb>
                <msb>9</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Legacy</name>
                    <description>Legacy / (EHTMU is bit 23 is set)</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>HtMf</name>
                    <description>HTMF  / (EhtTb is bit 23 is set)</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>HtGf</name>
                    <description>HTGF</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Vht</name>
                    <description>VHT</description>
                    <value>0x3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>HeSu</name>
                    <description>HESU</description>
                    <value>0x4</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>HeMu</name>
                    <description>HEMU</description>
                    <value>0x5</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>HeErSu</name>
                    <description>HEERSU</description>
                    <value>0x6</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>HeTb</name>
                    <description>HETB</description>
                    <value>0x7</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPDACHOLDOFF</name>
                <description>Selects DAC output hold-off</description>
                <lsb>10</lsb>
                <msb>10</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DacOutputHoldOffSpe</name>
                    <description>DAC output hold-off specified by WLANCTRLTXHOLDOFF</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>DacOutputHoldOffSpe1</name>
                    <description>DAC output hold-off specified by WLANCTRLTXHOLDOFF+WLANCTRLTXEXTRAHOLDOFF</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPPREAMBLESTART</name>
                <description>Selects condition to start the preamble generator</description>
                <lsb>11</lsb>
                <msb>11</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>StartPreambleGenerat</name>
                    <description>Start preamble generator after first byte of TX vector is received</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>StartPreambleGenerat1</name>
                    <description>Start preamble generator after first payload byte after the AMPDU delimiter is received</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPSIGNALBANDWIDTH</name>
                <description>Selects samples per symbol
          NOTE: signalbandwidth can have different value than channel bandwidth.
          Please sse the note for the WLANTXPCHANNELBANDWIDTH field.</description>
                <lsb>12</lsb>
                <msb>13</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>20Mhz</name>
                    <description>20MHz</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>40Mhz</name>
                    <description>40MHz</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>80Mhz</name>
                    <description>80MHz</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Reserve</name>
                    <description>This is reserved.</description>
                    <value>0x3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPCHANNELBANDWIDTH</name>
                <description>Selects samples per symbol
          NOTE: Channel bandwidth can have different value than signal bandwidth in case of Legacy packet type.
          For Legacy packet type signal bandwidth will always be 20MHz. In this case if channel bandwidth is
          set to 40MHz Legacy packet will be duplicated and if channel bandwidth is set to 80MHz Legacy packet
          will be copied over four segments. Duplication will be handled after TXP (IFFT) and TXP will perform
          coresponding scaling of I and Q components (over 52, 104 or 208 non-null sub-carriers).
          Channel bandwidth is not auto-configured and it should be configured to STA Operating bandwidth.</description>
                <lsb>14</lsb>
                <msb>15</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>20Mhz</name>
                    <description>20MHz</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>40Mhz</name>
                    <description>40MHz</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>80Mhz</name>
                    <description>80MHz</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Reserve</name>
                    <description>This is reserved.</description>
                    <value>0x3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPCHAINMODE</name>
                <description>Selects chain mode. HT-packets only.
          It determines the sign of pilots.</description>
                <lsb>16</lsb>
                <msb>17</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>1X1</name>
                    <description>1x1</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>2X2</name>
                    <description>2x2 (chain 1)</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>2X22</name>
                    <description>2x2 (chain 2)</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Reserve</name>
                    <description>This is reserved.</description>
                    <value>0x3</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPPILOTBYPASS</name>
                <description>Pilots insertion control.</description>
                <lsb>18</lsb>
                <msb>18</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>InsertPilots</name>
                    <description>Insert pilots</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>Bypass</name>
                    <description>Bypass</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPHELTFTYPE</name>
                <description>Type of HE-LTF preamble. For HE formats only.</description>
                <lsb>19</lsb>
                <msb>20</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>1XHeLtf</name>
                    <description>1x HE-LTF</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>2XHeLtf</name>
                    <description>2x HE-LTF</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>4XHeLtf</name>
                    <description>4x HE-LTF</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPHEGI</name>
                <description>Guard interval for HE frames.</description>
                <lsb>21</lsb>
                <msb>22</msb>
                <enumeratedValues>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>08Us</name>
                    <description>0.8us</description>
                    <value>0x0</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>16Us</name>
                    <description>1.6us</description>
                    <value>0x1</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                  <enumeratedValue>
                    <name>32Us</name>
                    <description>3.2us</description>
                    <value>0x2</value>
                  </enumeratedValue>
                </enumeratedValues>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANTXPPACKETTYPEEXT</name>
                <description>Selects packet type (this is MSB of this field):
          Packets 0-3 (Legacy, HTMF, HTGF, VHT) are in Pre-HE group with OFDM symbol
          length of 3.2us. HE packets have 12.8us OFDM symbol length.</description>
                <lsb>23</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
