                <description>Set EDCA BackOff Control to add/sub/replace mode</description>
                <lsb>0</lsb>
                <msb>1</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROLVALUE</name>
                <description>1. If BACKOFFCONTROLOPERATIONADD is set, Add value preset in WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROL (Bit's B2 to B16 ) to backOffNumber
          
          2. If BACKOFFCONTROLOPERATIONSUB is set, subtract backOffNumber from WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROL(Bit's B2 to B16) if
          backOffNumber is greater than equal to WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROL(Bit's B2 to B16) else replace backOffNumber with
          WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROL (Bit's B2 to B16)
          
          3. If BACKOFFCONTROLOPERATIONLIMITCHECKANDREPLACE is set, replace backOffNumber from WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROL(Bit's B17 to B23) if
          backOffNumber is greater than WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROL(Bit's B2 to B16)</description>
                <lsb>2</lsb>
                <msb>16</msb>
              </field>
              <field>
                <name>WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROLREPLACEVALUE</name>
                <description>If BACKOFFCONTROLOPERATIONLIMITCHECKANDREPLACE is set,replace backOffNumber from WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROL(Bit's B17 to B23) if
          backOffNumber is greater than WLANEDCABACKOFFCONTROL(Bit's B2 to B16)</description>
                <lsb>17</lsb>
                <msb>23</msb>
              </field>
            </fields>
          </register>
